2|//
3|// The program reads the sealed snapshot from /input/snapshot.json (or --input <file|dir>, or
4|// MAKEFUN_INPUT_DIR), scores every pre-token protocol with the model in lib/model.ts, writes the
5|// ranked board to /output/board.json, writes the dashboard's data to /output/data.js, copies this
6|// repository's dashboard/ and screenshots/ to /output, and last writes /output/dossier.json — the
7|// summary the judge reads — with the vendored make.fun library, exactly as the starter does.
8|//
9|// The dashboard is a static dark editorial page, no framework and no network: dashboard/index.html,
10|// dashboard/app.css and dashboard/app.js read data.js beside dashboard/, which this program writes
11|// from the same board the gate scores, so screenshots, page and board.json agree.
12|//
13|// Outside the grader's container the MAKEFUN_* variables stand in for the sealed mounts:
14|//   mkdir -p /tmp/tr-out && MAKEFUN_INPUT_DIR=input MAKEFUN_OUTPUT_DIR=/tmp/tr-out node main.ts
